 <div class="controls"><label>Index style<select bind:value={indexStyle}><option value="numeric">Numbers 1–14</option><option value="traditional">A, 2–10, P, N, Q, K</option></select></label><label>Card size<input aria-label="Card size" type="range" min="140" max="320" step="10" bind:value={size}/><span>{size}px</span></label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" bind:checked={grey}/> Grayscale check</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" bind:checked={upsideDown}/> Rotate cards 180°</label><label>Show suit<select bind:value={suit}><option value="all">All four suits</option>{#each suits as s}<option value={s}>{s}</option>{/each}</select></label></div>
 <div class="palette" aria-label="Suit colours">{#each suits as s}<div class="material"><img src={suitArtwork(base,s)} alt=""/><span>{s}</span><b>{SUIT_THEMES[s].material}</b></div>{/each}</div>
 <section><div class="section-heading"><h2>One rank, four suits</h2><label>Rank<select aria-label="Comparison rank" bind:value={sampleRank}>{#each Array.from({length:14},(_,i)=>i+1) as rank}<option value={rank}>{rank}{rank>10?` · ${['Page','Knight','Queen','King'][rank-11]}`:rank===1?' · Ace':''}</option>{/each}</select></label></div><div class="card-grid">{#each suits as s}{@const card=minor.find(c=>c.suit===s&&c.rank===Number(sampleRank))!}<figure><GameCard {card} design="indexed" {indexStyle}/><figcaption>{card.name}</figcaption></figure>{/each}</div></section>
 <section><h2>In a hand</h2><p>The fan exposes about a quarter of each card. The rank and suit should remain recognizable, including Page, Knight, Queen, and King.</p><div class="fan-scroll"><div class="fan">{#each fanCards as card,i}<div class="fan-card" style:z-index={i+1}><GameCard {card} design="indexed" {indexStyle}/></div>{/each}</div></div></section>
 <section><h2>Current and alternate</h2><div class="comparison"><figure><GameCard card={sample} design="classic"/><figcaption>Current · {sample.name}</figcaption></figure><figure><GameCard card={sample} design="indexed" {indexStyle}/><figcaption>Alternate · {sample.name}</figcaption></figure></div><p class="rank-key">Rank order: A is low; P (Page), N (Knight), Q (Queen), K (King) follow 10. Both ends repeat the same frame, label, index, and court artwork. Number cards show exactly their rank’s worth of main pips, excluding the corner indexes. Aces and other odd ranks have a single centre symbol.</p></section>
 <section class="court-review"><h2>Recomposed courts</h2><p>Portraits composed for the large corner indexes, with each held suit object visible beside its owner.</p><div class="card-grid">{#each minor.filter(c=>c.rank>10 && (suit==='all'||c.suit===suit)) as card}<figure><GameCard {card} design="indexed" {indexStyle}/><figcaption>{card.name}</figcaption></figure>{/each}</div></section>
 <section><h2>{suit==='all'?'The full playing deck':suit}</h2><p>{visible.length} cards. Check the two-digit ranks, both corners, and whether each suit remains easy to recognize at your preferred card size.</p><div class="card-grid deck">{#each visible as card}<figure><GameCard {card} design="indexed" {indexStyle}/><figcaption>{card.name}</figcaption></figure>{/each}</div></section>
</main>
